WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:04.070
Edward struggled to free himself from John and Frank.

2
00:00:04.071 --> 00:00:09.756
But they tightened their grips on his wrists and dragged him through the woods.

3
00:00:09.757 --> 00:00:12.658
"Let me go!" Edward cried.

4
00:00:12.659 --> 00:00:16.648
"Not after all the trouble we had finding you, my boy."

5
00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.474
John pinched Edward's arm with his other hand.

6
00:00:19.475 --> 00:00:26.233
"Ow!" Edward tried to kick Tom's father but missed.

7
00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:31.480
"In case you forgot, Ruffler put me in charge of you," Frank said.

8
00:00:31.481 --> 00:00:37.614
"He wasn't happy to hear you'd run off. From now on, you'll do what I say!"

9
00:00:37.615 --> 00:00:43.886
Edward didn't reply because he was busy plotting his escape.

10
00:00:43.887 --> 00:00:49.019
When they came upon another farmhouse, he hoped this was his opportunity.

11
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.820
But Frank had other ideas.

12
00:00:51.821 --> 00:00:55.869
"Here's your chance to be useful," Frank said.

13
00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:00.480
"Knock on the door, and if someone answers, beg for money or food.

14
00:01:00.481 --> 00:01:06.947
If no one's there, go into the kitchen and steal whatever you can."

15
00:01:06.948 --> 00:01:10.372
Edward grumbled as Frank shoved him toward the house.

16
00:01:10.373 --> 00:01:14.420
"And don't try any tricks!" Frank called out.

17
00:01:14.421 --> 00:01:18.688
Frank and John watched Edward knock on the door.

18
00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:22.525
When no one answered, he went inside.

19
00:01:22.526 --> 00:01:25.723
"He's not much of a beggar," John said.

20
00:01:25.724 --> 00:01:29.113
"And I need to work with him on stealing, but—"

21
00:01:29.114 --> 00:01:35.198
"Quiet!" Frank held up his hand. "What's he shouting about?"

22
00:01:35.199 --> 00:01:40.087
"Help! Is anybody home?" Edward cried.

23
00:01:40.088 --> 00:01:44.828
"I'm King Edward, and I've been kidnapped!"

24
00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:50.895
Frank and John ran for the house and dragged Edward outside.

25
00:01:50.896 --> 00:01:55.359
"That's exactly what I meant by tricks!" Frank snarled.

26
00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:00.137
"Next time I'll plan my escape more carefully," Edward thought.

27
00:02:00.138 --> 00:02:05.294
"And next time I'll succeed!"

28
00:02:05.295 --> 00:02:10.877
That night at the gang's campsite, Frank stepped on Edward's toes.

29
00:02:10.878 --> 00:02:14.119
Edward knew he'd done it on purpose.

30
00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:18.082
The third time it happened, Edward confronted Frank.

31
00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:21.603
"Stay away from my feet, you clumsy oaf!"

32
00:02:21.604 --> 00:02:27.173
Edward showered Frank with insults in English, Latin, and Greek.

33
00:02:27.174 --> 00:02:30.978
Everyone gathered around the two of them, clapping and cheering.

34
00:02:30.979 --> 00:02:35.140
"Hooray for the king!" they shouted.

35
00:02:35.141 --> 00:02:41.377
Two men lifted Edward onto their shoulders and paraded him around the camp.

36
00:02:41.378 --> 00:02:46.942
"Your son has quite a vocabulary," Ruffler said to John.

37
00:02:46.943 --> 00:02:51.049
"I taught him everything I know," John said modestly.

38
00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:56.517
"But I think he picked up a few words from books."

39
00:02:56.518 --> 00:03:01.175
Frank scowled as he watched everyone congratulating Edward.

40
00:03:01.176 --> 00:03:10.589
"I hope that boy is enjoying this," he thought, "because it's the last time he'll humiliate me!"

41
00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:16.371
The next afternoon the gang of beggars and thieves arrived at another village.

42
00:03:16.372 --> 00:03:20.854
"Don't come back empty-handed," Ruffler said to Edward.

43
00:03:20.855 --> 00:03:27.628
"And remember to obey Frank at all times."

44
00:03:27.629 --> 00:03:31.271
Frank walked up and down the streets with Edward.

45
00:03:31.272 --> 00:03:36.189
"Getting arrested might teach our young king a lesson," Frank thought.

46
00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:39.013
"But the others in the gang like him.

47
00:03:39.014 --> 00:03:43.672
So I can't be too obvious about my role in setting him up."

48
00:03:43.673 --> 00:03:49.163
While Frank was plotting his revenge, Edward was looking for a chance to escape.

49
00:03:49.164 --> 00:03:53.910
He thought about running when Frank bent over to pick up a penny on the street.

50
00:03:53.911 --> 00:03:57.656
"Not yet," Edward cautioned himself.

51
00:03:57.657 --> 00:04:02.142
"I have to wait for just the right moment."

52
00:04:02.143 --> 00:04:07.850
A few minutes later, they saw a woman carrying a fat package in a basket.

53
00:04:07.851 --> 00:04:13.655
"Stay here, and don't move until I come back," Frank said.

54
00:04:13.656 --> 00:04:16.206
"This is it!" Edward thought.

55
00:04:16.207 --> 00:04:21.992
But before Edward could run, Frank sneaked behind the woman and stole her package.

56
00:04:21.993 --> 00:04:24.634
He thrust it into Edward's hands.

57
00:04:24.635 --> 00:04:31.448
"Don't follow me!" Frank shouted to Edward as he ran away. "We'll meet up later."

58
00:04:31.449 --> 00:04:38.083
"No!" Edward threw the package on the ground, where it opened to reveal a ham.

59
00:04:38.084 --> 00:04:40.477
"I am not a thief!"

60
00:04:40.478 --> 00:04:47.333
"Oh yes, you are!" The woman grabbed Edward and shouted for help.

61
00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:53.777
Meanwhile Frank ran down an alley, from which he gleefully watched Edward's troubles unfold.

62
00:04:53.778 --> 00:04:57.791
"He'll soon be under arrest, and I'll be rid of him for good."

63
00:04:57.792 --> 00:05:04.785
Frank laughed as a blacksmith stepped out of his shop to help the woman.

64
00:05:04.786 --> 00:05:06.163
"What's the matter, ma'am?"

65
00:05:06.164 --> 00:05:10.883
The blacksmith picked up the ham and put it into the woman's basket.

66
00:05:10.884 --> 00:05:16.155
"I was walking home when this boy stole the ham right out of my basket!"

67
00:05:16.156 --> 00:05:22.970
"I am your king, not a thief." Edward pointed in the direction Frank had fled.

68
00:05:22.971 --> 00:05:29.821
"Quick! Go after Frank. He's the one who stole your ham!"

69
00:05:29.822 --> 00:05:33.855
"I'd better get out of here before the little traitor leads them to me."

70
00:05:33.856 --> 00:05:37.256
Frank smiled at the thought of Edward in jail.

71
00:05:37.257 --> 00:05:42.629
"Now I just have to think of something to tell Ruffler."

72
00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:49.174
Meanwhile Edward continued to struggle in the woman's grasp. "Let go of me!"

73
00:05:49.175 --> 00:05:54.969
"Be quiet!" The blacksmith reached out a strong arm for Edward.

74
00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:58.467
"I'm about to teach you a lesson!"

75
00:05:58.468 --> 00:06:08.899
"You'll do nothing of the kind!" A man suddenly grabbed the blacksmith.

